            <ArticleTitle>Computational analysis of platelet adhesion and aggregation under stagnation point flow conditions.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1-18</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The clinical relevance of platelet function assessment with stagnation point flow adhesio-aggregometry (SPAA) has been verified. Quantitative analysis of platelet adhesion and aggregation is possible by means of mathematical analysis of the dark-field, light intensity curves (growth curves) obtained during the SPAA experiment. We present a computational procedure for evaluating these curves, which was necessitated by, and is based on, actual clinical application. A qualitative growth curve classification, corresponding to a basic and distinct pattern of platelet deposition and characteristic of a regularly occurring clinical state is also presented.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
